      "page_title": "Closures, Traversal, and the Escape Ladder",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Closures Capture Too"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Capture mode is inferred from the body; `move` forces ownership.",
            "A `FnMut` closure holds its `&mut` capture for its whole life.",
            "Two closures capturing the same variable mutably is E0499.",
            "Scope them apart, or pass the state in as an argument."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mutate While Traversing",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`for x in &v { v.push(..) }` is **E0502** — collect changes, apply after.",
            "`retain`, `drain`, `dedup_by`, `swap_remove` edit in place safely.",
            "The ==Entry API== avoids a double lookup and a double borrow."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "map.entry(k)",
            "   .or_insert_with(Vec::new)",
            "   .push(v);   // one borrow",
            "v.retain(|x| *x > 0); // in place"
          ],
          "note": "no get-then-insert double borrow"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Escape Ladder",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "restructure",
              "return owned",
              "use indices",
              "`Rc`/`RefCell`",
              "`unsafe`"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Self-Referential Structs",
          "items": [
            "A struct holding a reference into itself is rejected outright.",
            "Fixes: store indices, `Rc`, an arena, or `Pin` plus unsafe.",
            "No annotation makes it typecheck — the shape is the problem."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Cloning Is Allowed",
          "text": "Cloning to satisfy the checker is legitimate for small values and cold paths. Measure before contorting a whole design around one borrow."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Moving The Check To Runtime",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Interior mutability = mutating through a `&T`.",
            "The aliasing rule still holds — enforced at runtime instead.",
            "`UnsafeCell<T>` is the only legal primitive for it.",
            "Every other cell type is built on top of `UnsafeCell`."
          ]
