    {
      "page_title": "Cell, RefCell, Rc, and Once Cells",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cell And RefCell",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Cell<T>`: get/set whole values, hands out no references.",
            "`Cell` is zero overhead but single-thread only.",
            "`RefCell<T>`: `borrow()` gives `Ref<T>`, `borrow_mut()` gives `RefMut<T>`.",
            "A runtime counter tracks who is currently borrowing."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let c = RefCell::new(vec![1]);",
            "c.borrow_mut().push(2);          // ok, guard drops",
            "let _a = c.borrow();",
            "// c.borrow_mut();  // panic: already borrowed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "A Panic Instead Of An Error",
          "text": "`RefCell` turns a compile error into a crash: \"already borrowed: BorrowMutError\". Use `try_borrow` / `try_borrow_mut` when you want a `Result` rather than a panic."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sharing The Ownership"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Rc<T>`: single-threaded shared ownership by reference count.",
            "`Rc<RefCell<T>>` is the canonical shared-mutable-graph pattern.",
            "`Arc<T>`: atomic refcount, safe to send across threads.",
            "`Arc<Mutex<T>>` or `Arc<RwLock<T>>` for cross-thread mutation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "When To Reach For It",
          "items": [
            "Only when the ownership graph is genuinely not a tree.",
            "A `RefCell` panic is the aliasing bug the compiler would have caught.",
            "Treat that panic as a design smell, not as the fix."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Leaks, Cows And Once Cells"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Rc` cycles leak: the count never reaches zero.",
            "Break a cycle with `Weak<T>` plus `upgrade()`.",
            "`Cow<'a,T>` borrows until a mutation is actually needed.",
            "`Cow::Borrowed` becomes `Cow::Owned` only on first write."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "static CFG: OnceLock<String> = OnceLock::new();",
            "CFG.get_or_init(|| load());  // write-once behind &self",
            "// LazyLock for the same thing with no explicit call"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
