      "page_title": "Two-Phase Borrows and the Map Insert Trap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Classic Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "v.push(v.len());          // ok: two-phase borrow",
            "map.insert(k, map[&k2]);  // E0502: no two-phase here",
            "let x = map[&k2]; map.insert(k, x);  // fix"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Fixing E0597, E0716, E0507, and E0521",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "E0502 In One Sentence",
          "text": "Copy the small read value out of the collection before the mutation, and the shared borrow is dead by the time the `&mut` starts."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Which fix do you try first?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Shorten the borrow — move or delete the later use.",
            "Split the data — disjoint fields or `split_at_mut`.",
            "Copy the small value out of the borrow.",
            "Restructure the ownership; clone only as the last step."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "E0597: Hoist It",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let r;",
            "{ let s = String::from(\"x\");",
            "  r = &s; }        // E0597",
            "println!(\"{r}\");"
          ],
          "note": "declare `s` in r's outer scope"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "E0716: Bind It",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let r = String::from(\"x\")",
            "    .as_str();       // E0716",
            "println!(\"{r}\");",
            "let s = String::from(\"x\");",
            "let r = s.as_str();  // fix"
          ],
          "note": "temporary dies at the semicolon"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "E0507: Take It",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "fn pop(&mut self) -> Option<T> {",
            "  let n = self.head.take()?;",
            "  // self.head.unwrap() → E0507",
            "  self.head = n.next;",
            "  Some(n.val)",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "`take()` leaves `None` behind"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "E0521: Own It",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "fn f(v: &Vec<i32>) {",
            "  thread::spawn(move || v.len());",
            "  // E0521: v escapes the fn",
            "}",
            "// fix: take Vec<i32>, or clone"
          ],
          "note": "spawn demands `'static` data"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Name The Broken Rule",
          "items": [
            "Either a referent died before its reference, or",
            "an exclusive borrow overlapped another borrow.",
            "Every one of these codes is one of those two."
          ],
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Can the later use move **earlier**?",
            "Are the two borrows on disjoint fields?",
            "Is the value small and `Copy`?",
            "Only then reach for `clone()`."
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
